From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Tue, 29 Sep 2026 00:42:08 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Default to a 480 KiB stack limit

The engine is built without the debugging dumps now (NDEBUG), which
shrinks the interpreter's frame on the WASM stack by 16 bytes (272 to
256 bytes per level of plain recursion), so recursion at the same limit
goes 3-6% deeper (plain recursion 1924 to 2045 levels at 512 KiB, the
getter pattern 1635 to 1722). The default only just fit Node.js's main
thread: with the new build the getter, apply, JSON, proxy, toString and
generator recursions of test/stack.test.ts overflow its 984 KB host stack
before QuickJS's limit is reached.

At 480 KiB the depth is what it was (plain 1917 levels, getter 1615).
---
 src/index.ts       | 2 +-
 test/stack.test.ts | 4 ++--
 2 files changed, 3 insertions(+), 3 deletions(-)

diff --git a/src/index.ts b/src/index.ts
index 25c1010..aacf242 100644
--- a/src/index.ts
+++ b/src/index.ts
@@ -55,7 +55,7 @@ export const MAX_STACK_SIZE = 1024 * 1024;
  * exceeded" before a 1 MiB host native stack overflows. Raise it up to
  * {@link MAX_STACK_SIZE} on hosts with a larger native stack.
  */
-export const DEFAULT_STACK_SIZE = 512 * 1024;
+export const DEFAULT_STACK_SIZE = 480 * 1024;
 
 /**
  * A host callback behind a QuickJS function (`vm.newFunction()`).
diff --git a/test/stack.test.ts b/test/stack.test.ts
index e2ee282..681ae24 100644
--- a/test/stack.test.ts
+++ b/test/stack.test.ts
@@ -43,9 +43,9 @@ const runInWorker = (script: string, stackSizeMb: number): Promise<Record<string
   });
 
 describe('stack limits', () => {
-  it('allows up to 1 MiB, and defaults to 512 KiB', async () => {
+  it('allows up to 1 MiB, and defaults to 480 KiB', async () => {
     expect(MAX_STACK_SIZE).toBe(1024 * 1024);
-    expect(DEFAULT_STACK_SIZE).toBe(512 * 1024);
+    expect(DEFAULT_STACK_SIZE).toBe(480 * 1024);
     using vm = await QuickJS.create({ wasm, maxStackSize: MAX_STACK_SIZE });
     expect(vm.evalCode('1 + 1').consume((h) => h.toNumber())).toBe(2);
     await expect(QuickJS.create({ wasm, maxStackSize: MAX_STACK_SIZE + 1 })).rejects.toThrow(/maxStackSize/);
